---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import requirements from '../data/requirements.json';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is a photo and signature resizer?',
    a: 'A photo and signature resizer prepares your photo or signature for an online form. DocCheck combines a photo and signature checker with a fixing tool: select your exact form, upload your file, and it checks file size, dimensions, format and aspect ratio against that form\u2019s published requirements, identifies which requirement fails, automatically fixes supported issues, verifies the corrected file again, and gives you the fixed file to download. The core check-and-fix process runs in your browser.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I resize a photo for an online exam form?',
    a: 'Select the exact exam form in the checker above \u2014 for example SSC CGL 2026 photo \u2014 upload your photo, and click Fix automatically. The exam photo resizer adjusts dimensions, compresses the file into the required KB window and converts it to the required format, then verifies the fixed file before download. Always confirm the final file on the live application portal.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I resize a signature for an online application?',
    a: 'Select the signature entry for your form \u2014 for example SSC CGL 2026 signature \u2014 and upload a clear scan in black or blue ink on white paper. DocCheck checks its size, dimensions and format, then the fixing tool compresses it into the required KB window, preserves the required shape and converts it to JPG where needed, verifies the result again, and lets you download it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I reduce a photo to the required KB size?',
    a: 'Check the photo first to see how far over the maximum it is \u2014 phone cameras often produce 1 to 5 MB files when a typical government exam photo size is 20 to 50 KB. Then click Fix automatically: the photo size reducer and photo compressor for exam compress the image step by step into the selected form\u2019s KB window and re-verify it. If your file is below the minimum, it is flagged instead, because over-compressed images can lose quality.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I reduce a signature to the required KB size?',
    a: 'Upload the signature under its exact form entry to see its current KB size against the required minimum and maximum of that typical government exam signature size window. Fix automatically then compresses the signature image into that window and converts it to the required format where supported. Use a clean scan on white paper so compression keeps the signature readable, and verify the fixed file before downloading.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I resize a photo to the required pixel dimensions?',
    a: 'Upload the photo under your exact form to see your pixels side by side with the required pixels \u2014 for example, DocCheck lists the SSC CGL 2026 photo as 100 by 100 px. Fix automatically resizes to those exact pixels where the requirement uses pixels. Where a form specifies cm or mm, the image size reducer preserves the required ratio and compresses into the KB bounds, then shows the new dimensions for verification.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I check if my photo meets an exam\u2019s requirements?',
    a: 'Select your category and the exact form and notification in the checker, then upload your photo. The photo requirements checker reads its KB size, pixel dimensions, format and aspect ratio where applicable, compares each value with the published exam photo requirements for that form, and shows which checks pass and which need fixing, with the official source and verification date alongside.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I check if my signature meets an exam\u2019s requirements?',
    a: 'Select the signature entry for your exact form and notification, then upload your signature scan. The signature size checker reads its KB size, dimensions and format, compares each against that form\u2019s published signature limits, and identifies exactly which requirement fails so you can fix it before uploading to the portal.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I check photo and signature size before uploading?',
    a: 'Use the photo upload checker above before visiting the portal. Choose the form, upload the file, and DocCheck reads its file size, dimensions and format locally in your browser and compares each against the selected requirement. You see your values next to the required values, so you know what to fix instead of facing a rejection after submission.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I resize and compress a photo online for government exams?',
    a: 'Yes. DocCheck works as a photo resizer for government exams with JPG, JPEG and PNG photos in your browser and no sign-up. After checking, Fix automatically resizes, compresses and converts supported files into the selected form\u2019s limits and verifies the result for download. PDF files show size information only and need to be converted to JPG first.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I resize a signature online for government exams?',
    a: 'Yes. Select the signature entry for your exam, upload your scanned signature, and this exam photo and signature resizer applies the same flow: check size, dimensions and format, identify failures, compress and convert supported files, verify the corrected file again, and provide it for download. Scans should use dark ink on plain white paper for the best result.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What should I do if my photo is too large for an exam form?',
    a: 'Select your exact form, upload the photo to confirm by how much it exceeds the maximum, then click Fix automatically to compress it into the allowed KB window, correct dimensions and convert the format where supported. Verify the fixed file in the before-and-after panel before downloading. If the shape or background is wrong, retake the photo with the required background rather than stretching it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What should I do if my signature file is too large?',
    a: 'Check the signature under its exact form entry to see the required maximum, then run Fix automatically to compress it into that window and convert it to the required format. If the scan is still too large or blurry, rescan at a lower resolution in black or blue ink on white paper and check again. The corrected file is verified before download.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I check the file size, dimensions and format of a photo?',
    a: 'Yes. The photo size checker reads all three from your uploaded photo: KB size, pixel dimensions and format, plus aspect ratio where the form requires a shape such as 1 by 1. Each value is shown next to the requirement for the form you selected, with a pass or fail status.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I check the file size, dimensions and format of a signature?',
    a: 'Yes. The signature size checker reads the KB size, dimensions and format of your uploaded signature and compares each against the signature limits of the form you selected. Failures are identified row by row so you know whether size, shape or format needs fixing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does DocCheck automatically fix photo and signature requirements?',
    a: 'Where supported, yes. For JPG, JPEG and PNG photos and signatures, Fix automatically resizes dimensions, compresses KB size and converts format in one pass, then re-verifies the corrected file. Not everything can be fixed automatically: PDF files show size information only, and issues like a wrong background, face position or an unverified requirement still need your attention, and the live portal remains the final authority.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can DocCheck verify the file after resizing it?',
    a: 'Yes. After Fix automatically runs, DocCheck reads the corrected file again and re-runs the same checks for size, dimensions and format. A before-and-after panel shows the original next to the fixed file with its new KB size, dimensions and format, plus an updated pass and fail ledger, so you only download a file you have seen verified.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does DocCheck support SSC photo and signature requirements?',
    a: 'Yes. DocCheck includes SSC CGL 2026 entries: the SSC photo size is listed as 20 to 50 KB, JPG or JPEG, 100 by 100 px with a 1 by 1 ratio, verified against the official notification, and the SSC signature size is listed as 10 to 20 KB, JPG or JPEG with a 2 by 1 shape. The SSC signature record notes that the notification\u2019s sections state slightly different figures, so use the SSC photo resizer and SSC signature resizer entries in the checker and follow what the live SSC portal shows.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does DocCheck support UPSC photo and signature requirements?',
    a: 'Yes. DocCheck includes UPSC CSE 2026 photo and signature entries, currently listed as JPG or JPEG with the UPSC photo size between 20 and 50 KB and the signature between 10 and 20 KB. These records are marked as needing recheck because limits can differ by notification and cycle, so select the relevant UPSC form, use the UPSC photo resizer and UPSC signature resizer checks, and confirm on the live UPSC portal.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does DocCheck support IBPS photo and signature requirements?',
    a: 'Yes. DocCheck includes IBPS PO 2026 photo and signature entries, currently listed as JPG or JPEG with the IBPS photo size between 20 and 50 KB and the signature between 10 and 20 KB in black ink on white paper. These records are marked as needing recheck because IBPS guidance can vary, so select the relevant IBPS form, use the IBPS photo resizer and IBPS signature resizer checks, and verify against the live IBPS portal and notification.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does DocCheck support RRB photo and signature requirements?',
    a: 'Yes, but RRB limits vary by notification. DocCheck includes RRB NTPC 2026 photo and signature entries marked as needing recheck, without fixed KB or pixel values in the current data. Select the relevant RRB form in the checker, review its published requirements and source note, and always follow the exact limits shown on the live RRB portal for your notification.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I resize a passport photo for an application?',
    a: 'Yes. DocCheck includes an Indian Passport photo entry listed as 51 by 51 mm with a 1 by 1 ratio, JPG or JPEG, plain white background and full face visible, following Passport Seva guidance. Select Indian Passport photo in the checker, upload your image, and the passport photo resizer crops toward the required square shape, resizes and converts to JPG, then verifies the result for download.',
  },
];

const title = 'Photo and Signature Resizer – Check, Fix & Verify | DocCheck';
const description =
  'Free photo and signature resizer — check photo and signature size, auto-fix, verify and download for SSC, UPSC, IBPS, RRB and passport uploads.';
const keywords =
  'photo and signature resizer, photo and signature checker, photo signature size checker, photo size checker, signature size checker, photo resizer for government exams, signature resizer for government exams, exam photo resizer, exam photo and signature resizer, photo size reducer, image size reducer, photo compressor for exam, photo resize online, signature resize online, photo requirements checker, exam photo requirements, photo upload checker, government exam photo size, government exam signature size';
const canonical = 'https://www.exampicfix.in/';
const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'DocCheck — Photo and Signature Resizer',
    url: 'https://www.exampicfix.in/',
    applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Web browser',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'INR' },
    featureList: 'Check photo size, check signature size, automatically fix and resize, verify corrected file, download fixed file',
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://www.exampicfix.in/' }],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
    })),
  },
];

const categories = [
  {
    id: 'exam',
    label: 'Exams',
    hint: 'SSC · UPSC · IBPS · RRB · NTA',
    icon: '<svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 9L12 4 2 9l10 5 10-5z"/><path d="M6 11.5V16c0 1.5 2.7 3 6 3s6-1.5 6-3v-4.5"/><path d="M22 9v5"/></svg>',
  },
  {
    id: 'identity_document',
    label: 'Identity Documents',
    hint: 'PAN · Voter ID · Passport · Aadhaar',
    icon: '<svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="5" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="2"/><path d="M5.5 16c.6-1.4 1.5-2 2.5-2s1.9.6 2.5 2"/><path d="M14 9h5M14 13h5"/></svg>',
  },
  {
    id: 'bank_kyc',
    label: 'Bank & KYC',
    hint: 'Account opening · Mutual fund KYC',
    icon: '<svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 9l9-6 9 6"/><path d="M4 9v10M20 9v10M8 12v5M12 12v5M16 12v5"/><path d="M2 20h20"/></svg>',
  },
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} keywords={keywords} canonical={canonical} schema={schema}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <h1>Photo and Signature Resizer — Check, Fix, Verify & Download</h1>
        <p class="lede">Free <strong>photo and signature resizer</strong> and <strong>photo and signature checker</strong> for government exams and ID applications. <strong>Check photo size</strong> and <strong>signature size</strong>, automatically resize and compress, verify the fixed file, then download — all in your browser.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="#check" style="text-decoration:none;text-align:center;">Check a File</a>
          <a href="/requirements/">Browse Requirements</a>
        </div>
        <p class="trustline">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" style="flex:none;margin-top:3px;"><rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 018 0v3"/></svg>
          Your file stays in your browser during the core check-and-fix process.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="verify-fig" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 300 190">
          <rect x="70" y="8" width="160" height="158" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/>
          <rect x="95" y="28" width="110" height="104" rx="4" fill="var(--surface-2)" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="103" y="36" width="34" height="44" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="var(--authority)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="120" cy="52" r="7" fill="none" stroke="var(--authority)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <path d="M110 72c2-5 5-7 10-7s8 2 10 7" fill="none" stroke="var(--authority)" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="145" y="38" width="52" height="7" rx="2" fill="var(--line)"/>
          <rect x="145" y="51" width="40" height="7" rx="2" fill="var(--line)"/>
          <rect x="145" y="64" width="46" height="7" rx="2" fill="var(--line)"/>
          <rect x="103" y="92" width="94" height="7" rx="2" fill="var(--line)"/>
          <rect x="103" y="105" width="70" height="7" rx="2" fill="var(--line)"/>
          <rect x="103" y="118" width="80" height="7" rx="2" fill="var(--line)"/>
          <rect class="scanline" x="95" y="28" width="110" height="3" fill="var(--authority)"/>
          <g class="scancheck">
            <circle cx="216" cy="142" r="17" fill="var(--pass-bg)" stroke="var(--pass)" stroke-width="2.5"/>
            <path d="M208 142l6 6 12-13" fill="none" stroke="var(--pass)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </g>
          <text class="scanready" x="150" y="182" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="var(--pass)">✓ READY</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Upload → Check → Verify → Ready</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="check" aria-label="File checker">
    <p class="progressline" id="progressLine" aria-live="polite">Category — · Form — · File —</p>
    <p class="stateline" id="appStatus">Starting… (if this never changes, JavaScript is blocked in your browser)</p>

    <noscript>
      <p class="verdict fail"><span class="v-title">❌ JavaScript is off</span><span class="v-sub">DOCHECK needs JavaScript turned on to read and fix your file, because everything runs in your browser. Turn it on and reload.</span></p>
    </noscript>

    <script type="application/json" id="requirements-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(requirements).replace(/</g, '\\u003c')}></script>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step" id="step1">
        <p class="step-title">Choose category</p>
        <p class="step-sub">What is this file for?</p>
        <div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose category">
          {categories.map((c) => (
            <button type="button" class="choice" data-cat={c.id} aria-pressed="false">
              <span set:html={c.icon} />
              {c.label}<small>{c.hint}</small>
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step" id="step2">
        <p class="step-title">Choose the form you're applying for</p>
        <p class="step-sub">Search, then pick one.</p>
        <label for="formSearch">Search forms</label>
        <input id="formSearch" type="search" placeholder="Type to filter — e.g. SSC, PAN, passport…" disabled autocomplete="off" />
        <div class="formlist" id="formList">
          <p class="hint" id="formHint">Choose a category above first.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="selected-line" id="selectedLine" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </li>
      <li class="step" id="step3">
        <p class="step-title">Upload your file</p>
        <p class="step-sub">JPG, JPEG or PNG photo/signature. PDF shows size info only.</p>
        <label class="dropzone" id="dropzone" for="file">
          <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 16V4M7 9l5-5 5 5"/><path d="M4 16v3a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2v-3"/></svg>
          <span class="dz-title">Drop your file here, or choose from your device</span>
          <span class="dz-sub">Works with camera photos and gallery images on mobile.</span>
          <input id="file" type="file" accept="image/*,.pdf" disabled />
        </label>
        <p class="hint" id="fileHint">Choose a category and form above to enable upload.</p>
        <div class="filecard" id="fileCard" hidden>
          <img id="fileThumb" alt="" />
          <div class="fmeta">
            <div class="fname" id="fileName"></div>
            <div class="num" id="fileMeta"></div>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="linkbtn" id="removeFile">Remove</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step" id="step4">
        <p class="step-title">Check, fix &amp; download</p>
        <p class="hint" id="resultsEmpty">Your check result will appear here after you upload a file.</p>
        <span id="verdict" class="verdict" hidden aria-live="polite"></span>
        <p class="matchline" id="matchLine" hidden aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="report" id="ledger" hidden>
          <div class="report-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Your file</span><span>Requirement</span><span>Status</span></div>
          <div id="ledgerBody"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="fixbox" id="fixBox" hidden>
          <p><strong>Fix automatically.</strong> Resize, compress or convert this file to meet the selected requirements.</p>
          <div class="btn-row sticky-action">
            <button type="button" class="btn-primary" id="fixBtn" disabled>Fix automatically</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-grid" id="beforeAfter" hidden>
          <figure class="ba-card">
            <figcaption>Before</figcaption>
            <img id="beforeImg" alt="Your uploaded file" />
            <dl id="beforeMeta">
              <dt>Size</dt><dd id="bSize">—</dd>
              <dt>Dimensions</dt><dd id="bDims">—</dd>
              <dt>Format</dt><dd id="bFormat">—</dd>
            </dl>
          </figure>
          <div class="ba-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <figure class="ba-card fixed">
            <figcaption>Fixed file</figcaption>
            <img id="afterImg" alt="Corrected file preview" />
            <dl id="afterMeta">
              <dt>Size</dt><dd id="aSize">—</dd>
              <dt>Dimensions</dt><dd id="aDims">—</dd>
              <dt>Format</dt><dd id="aFormat">—</dd>
            </dl>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row" id="downloadRow" hidden>
          <button type="button" class="btn-primary" id="downloadBtn" disabled>Download File</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-ghost" id="checkAnotherBtn">Check Another File</button>
          <p class="hint" id="downloadNote"></p>
        </div>
        <div id="trust"></div>
        <p class="fineprint" id="accuracyNote"></p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Browse exam photo requirements" data-reveal>
    <h2>Browse exam photo requirements</h2>
    <ul class="reflist">
      {requirements.map((r) => (
        <li><a href={`/requirements/${r.slug}/`}>{r.form_name} — {r.document_type}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <a class="tool-link-card" data-reveal href="/resize-image-online/">
    <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6"/><path d="M9 21H3v-6"/><path d="M21 3l-7 7"/><path d="M3 21l7-7"/></svg>
    <span>Need to resize an image for something else? Try our free custom image resizer</span>
    <span class="tl-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
  </a>

  <section class="prose" aria-label="About this photo and signature resizer" data-reveal>
    <h2>What this photo and signature resizer does</h2>
    <p>DocCheck is a <strong>photo and signature checker</strong> combined with an automatic fixing tool. You select the exact form you are applying for, upload your photo or signature, and the tool checks your file against that form's published requirements. When a problem is found, it identifies exactly which value failed — file size, dimensions, format or aspect ratio — and, where supported, fixes it automatically. The corrected file is then verified again against the same requirements before you download it.</p>
    <p>The full flow is: <strong>check → find the problem → automatically fix → verify the fixed file → download</strong>. Nothing is reduced to a simple pass/fail badge: every result shows your file's values side by side with the required values, so you always know what changed and why.</p>
    <h2>How the photo size checker and signature size checker work</h2>
    <p>Every upload is read locally in your browser across five checks:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>File size check.</strong> Your file's KB size is compared against the form's minimum and maximum — for example, many exam photos must fall between 20 KB and 50 KB. Phone cameras typically produce 1–5 MB files, so the <strong>photo size reducer</strong> and <strong>photo compressor for exam</strong> use shrink oversized images into the allowed window.</li>
      <li><strong>Dimension check.</strong> Pixel, cm or mm dimensions are read from the image. Where a form demands exact pixels (such as 100 × 100 px), the <strong>exam photo resizer</strong> resizes precisely; where a form specifies physical units, the tool preserves the required ratio and compresses into the KB bounds.</li>
      <li><strong>Format check.</strong> Most portals accept only JPG or JPEG. PNG, HEIC and PDF uploads are flagged, and the automatic fix converts images to JPG when the requirement calls for it.</li>
      <li><strong>Aspect-ratio check.</strong> Square photos (1:1), 2:1 signatures and 51 × 51 mm passport frames each need the right shape. The <strong>image size reducer</strong> crops and resizes while keeping faces and signatures centred.</li>
      <li><strong>Application-specific check.</strong> Each form carries its own sourced limits — background rules, special portal notes and verification dates. Selecting the right form matters: an <a href="/ssc-photo-and-signature-resizer/">SSC photo and signature resizer</a> check uses different bounds than a <a href="/passport-photo-resizer/">passport photo size checker</a> check.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Automatic fix, verify and download</h2>
    <p>When your file fails a supported check, click <strong>Fix automatically</strong>. The tool resizes dimensions, compresses KB size and converts format in one pass, then immediately re-runs the <strong>photo requirements checker</strong> on the corrected file. A before-and-after panel shows the original next to the fixed file with its new size, dimensions and format, so you can confirm the fix before downloading. The download button saves the verified file to your device, ready for the portal.</p>
    <p>Automatic fixing covers JPG, JPEG and PNG photos and signatures. PDF files show size information only and cannot yet be auto-fixed — convert them to JPG first. DocCheck never replaces the official portal: it prepares your file against the selected form's published requirements, and the live portal remains the final authority.</p>
    <h2>Government exam and application photo requirements</h2>
    <p>Government portals are strict because automated validators reject anything outside the published <strong>exam photo requirements</strong>. Typical <strong>government exam photo size</strong> limits are JPG/JPEG between 20 KB and 50 KB with a white background, while <strong>government exam signature size</strong> limits are commonly 10–20 KB in black or blue ink on white paper. Exact pixel or cm dimensions, ratios and backgrounds differ per notification and can change yearly — which is why checking against the selected form, rather than guessing, saves a rejected application.</p>
    <p>Use the dedicated resizers for your exam:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/ssc-photo-and-signature-resizer/">SSC photo and signature resizer</a> — SSC photo size and SSC signature size for SSC CGL.</li>
      <li><a href="/upsc-photo-and-signature-resizer/">UPSC photo and signature resizer</a> — UPSC photo size and signature checks for UPSC CSE.</li>
      <li><a href="/ibps-photo-and-signature-resizer/">IBPS photo and signature resizer</a> — IBPS photo size and signature checks for IBPS PO.</li>
      <li><a href="/rrb-photo-and-signature-resizer/">RRB photo and signature resizer</a> — RRB photo size and signature checks for RRB NTPC.</li>
      <li><a href="/passport-photo-resizer/">Passport photo resizer</a> — 51 × 51 mm passport photo size checker for Indian Passport.</li>
      <li><a href="/exam-photo-and-signature-resizer/">Exam photo and signature resizer hub</a> and <a href="/photo-resizer-for-government-exams/">photo resizer for government exams</a> guide for all exams.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Common upload problems this photo upload checker catches</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Wrong KB size.</strong> Camera photos far above the maximum, or over-compressed scans below the minimum. The photo size reducer compresses or flags quality loss.</li>
      <li><strong>Wrong dimensions.</strong> Selfies and crops that don't match the required pixels, cm or ratio. The exam photo resizer corrects shape and size.</li>
      <li><strong>Wrong format.</strong> PNG or HEIC instead of JPG/JPEG. The signature resize online and photo resize online fix converts to the required format.</li>
      <li><strong>Wrong aspect ratio or background.</strong> Non-square photos, stretched signatures, or dark backgrounds where white is required — flagged before submission.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Checking takes seconds and happens entirely on your device. Learn more about the process on the <a href="/how-it-works/">how it works</a> page, browse every limit on the <a href="/requirements/">requirements</a> page, or jump straight to the <a href="/#check">photo upload checker</a> above.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose" aria-label="Frequently asked questions" data-reveal>
    <h2>Photo and signature resizer — FAQs</h2>
    <Faq items={faqs} />
  </section>

  <script>
    import { readFileProps, checkAgainstRequirement, fixImage } from '../lib/engine.ts';

    const requirements = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('requirements-data').textContent);

    const catBtns = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[data-cat]'));
    const formSearch = document.getElementById('formSearch');
    const formList = document.getElementById('formList');
    const selectedLine = document.getElementById('selectedLine');
    const dropzone = document.getElementById('dropzone');
    const fileInput = document.getElementById('file');
    const fileHint = document.getElementById('fileHint');
    const fileCard = document.getElementById('fileCard');
    const fileThumb = document.getElementById('fileThumb');
    const fileName = document.getElementById('fileName');
    const fileMeta = document.getElementById('fileMeta');
    const removeFile = document.getElementById('removeFile');
    const verdict = document.getElementById('verdict');
    const trust = document.getElementById('trust');
    const ledger = document.getElementById('ledger');
    const ledgerBody = document.getElementById('ledgerBody');
    const resultsEmpty = document.getElementById('resultsEmpty');
    const fixBox = document.getElementById('fixBox');
    const fixBtn = document.getElementById('fixBtn');
    const downloadRow = document.getElementById('downloadRow');
    const downloadBtn = document.getElementById('downloadBtn');
    const checkAnotherBtn = document.getElementById('checkAnotherBtn');
    const downloadNote = document.getElementById('downloadNote');
    const beforeAfter = document.getElementById('beforeAfter');
    const beforeImg = document.getElementById('beforeImg');
    const afterImg = document.getElementById('afterImg');
    const accuracyNote = document.getElementById('accuracyNote');
    const progressLine = document.getElementById('progressLine');
    const step1 = document.getElementById('step1');
    const step2 = document.getElementById('step2');
    const step3 = document.getElementById('step3');

    let activeCat = '';
    let currentReq = null;
    let currentFile = null;
    let fixedBlob = null;
    let fixedUrl = null;
    let thumbUrl = null;

    document.getElementById('appStatus').textContent = '✓ Ready — choose a category above to begin.';

    if (!window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches && 'IntersectionObserver' in window) {
      const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach((e) => { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); } });
      }, { threshold: 0.1 });
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]').forEach((el) => { el.classList.add('reveal'); io.observe(el); });
    }

    function updateMatchLine(rows) {
      const matchLine = document.getElementById('matchLine');
      const passed = rows.filter((r) => r.pass === true).length;
      const failed = rows.filter((r) => r.pass === false).length;
      matchLine.hidden = false;
      matchLine.innerHTML = '';
      const ok = document.createElement('span');
      ok.className = 'ok';
      ok.textContent = `✓ ${passed} check${passed === 1 ? '' : 's'} passed`;
      const sep = document.createTextNode(' · ');
      const bad = document.createElement('span');
      bad.className = 'bad';
      bad.textContent = failed === 0 ? '✓ nothing to fix' : `✗ ${failed} need${failed === 1 ? 's' : ''} fixing`;
      matchLine.append(ok, sep, bad);
    }

    function statusLabel(r) {
      if (r.status === 'verified') return 'verified';
      if (r.status === 'known_discrepancy') return 'see note';
      return 'needs recheck';
    }

    function updateProgress() {
      const tick = (v) => (v ? '✓' : '—');
      progressLine.textContent =
        `Category ${tick(activeCat)} · Form ${tick(currentReq)} · File ${tick(currentFile)}`;
      step1.classList.toggle('done', !!activeCat);
      step2.classList.toggle('done', !!currentReq);
      step3.classList.toggle('done', !!currentFile);
    }

    function renderFormList(q) {
      const query = (q || '').toLowerCase();
      const list = requirements.filter(
        (r) => r.category === activeCat && (!query || `${r.form_name} ${r.document_type}`.toLowerCase().includes(query)),
      );
      formList.innerHTML = '';
      if (!list.length) {
        const p = document.createElement('p');
        p.className = 'hint';
        p.textContent = 'No match. Try a different search.';
        formList.appendChild(p);
        return;
      }
      list.forEach((r) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.type = 'button';
        b.className = 'formbtn' + (currentReq && currentReq.id === r.id ? ' active' : '');
        b.dataset.id = r.id;
        const wrap = document.createElement('span');
        const name = document.createElement('span');
        name.className = 'fname';
        name.textContent = r.form_name;
        const meta = document.createElement('span');
        meta.className = 'fmeta';
        meta.textContent = `${r.document_type} · ${r.category === 'exam' ? 'Exam' : r.category === 'identity_document' ? 'Identity document' : 'Bank & KYC'}`;
        wrap.append(name, meta);
        const badge = document.createElement('span');
        badge.className = `badge ${r.status}`;
        badge.textContent = statusLabel(r);
        b.append(wrap, badge);
        b.addEventListener('click', () => selectForm(r.id));
        formList.appendChild(b);
      });
    }

    function resetResults() {
      verdict.hidden = true;
      ledger.hidden = true;
      fixBox.hidden = true;
      downloadRow.hidden = true;
      beforeAfter.hidden = true;
      resultsEmpty.hidden = false;
      document.getElementById('matchLine').hidden = true;
      accuracyNote.textContent = '';
      downloadNote.textContent = '';
      delete document.body.dataset.result;
      document.body.dataset.stage = currentReq ? 'form' : activeCat ? 'category' : '';
      fixedBlob = null;
      if (fixedUrl) { URL.revokeObjectURL(fixedUrl); fixedUrl = null; }
    }

    function renderTrust() {
      trust.innerHTML = '';
      if (!currentReq) return;
      const card = document.createElement('div');
      const needsRecheck = currentReq.status === 'needs_recheck';
      card.className = 'source-card' + (needsRecheck ? ' recheck' : '');
      const label = document.createElement('div');
      label.className = 's-label';
      label.textContent = needsRecheck ? 'UNVERIFIED — NEEDS RECHECK' : 'OFFICIAL SOURCE — VERIFIED REQUIREMENT';
      const dl = document.createElement('dl');
      const add = (term, text) => {
        const dt = document.createElement('dt');
        dt.textContent = term;
        const dd = document.createElement('dd');
        dd.textContent = text;
        dl.append(dt, dd);
      };
      add('Source', currentReq.official_source);
      add('Last verified', currentReq.verified_date ?? 'Not yet verified — marked needs recheck');
      if (currentReq.source_url) {
        const dt = document.createElement('dt');
        dt.textContent = 'Official page';
        const dd = document.createElement('dd');
        const a = document.createElement('a');
        a.href = currentReq.source_url;
        a.rel = 'noopener';
        a.textContent = 'View official source →';
        dd.appendChild(a);
        dl.append(dt, dd);
      }
      if (needsRecheck) add('Note', 'This record is not yet verified against a current official source. Use the live portal as the authority.');
      card.append(label, dl);
      trust.appendChild(card);
      if (currentReq.status === 'known_discrepancy') {
        const d = document.createElement('div');
        d.className = 'discrepancy';
        const l = document.createElement('div');
        l.className = 's-label';
        l.textContent = '⚠ SOURCE DISCREPANCY';
        const p1 = document.createElement('p');
        p1.textContent = 'Two official references list different values for this requirement.';
        const p2 = document.createElement('p');
        p2.textContent = currentReq.discrepancy_note;
        const p3 = document.createElement('p');
        p3.innerHTML = '';
        p3.textContent = 'Recommendation: follow the requirement shown on the live application portal when available.';
        d.append(l, p1, p2, p3);
        trust.appendChild(d);
      }
    }

    function clearFile(message) {
      fileInput.value = '';
      currentFile = null;
      if (thumbUrl) { URL.revokeObjectURL(thumbUrl); thumbUrl = null; }
      fileCard.hidden = true;
      fileHint.textContent = message || 'Ready — choose your photo, signature, or document file.';
      updateProgress();
    }

    function selectForm(id, opts) {
      currentReq = requirements.find((r) => r.id === id) || null;
      formList.querySelectorAll('[data-id]').forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle('active', x.dataset.id === id));
      if (!currentReq) return;
      selectedLine.textContent = `Selected: ${currentReq.form_name} — ${currentReq.document_type}`;
      fileInput.disabled = false;
      fileHint.textContent = 'Ready — choose your photo, signature, or document file.';
      resetResults();
      renderTrust();
      updateProgress();
      if (!opts || !opts.keepFile) clearFile();
      else if (currentFile) handleFile();
    }

    catBtns.forEach((b) => {
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        activeCat = b.dataset.cat;
        catBtns.forEach((x) => {
          const on = x === b;
          x.classList.toggle('active', on);
          x.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
        });
        currentReq = null;
        selectedLine.textContent = '';
        fileInput.disabled = true;
        formSearch.disabled = false;
        formSearch.value = '';
        resetResults();
        renderTrust();
        clearFile('Now choose a specific form below to enable upload.');
        fileInput.disabled = true;
        renderFormList('');
        updateProgress();
        formSearch.focus();
      });
    });

    formSearch.addEventListener('input', () => renderFormList(formSearch.value));

    function showFileCard(f, dimsText) {
      if (thumbUrl) URL.revokeObjectURL(thumbUrl);
      fileCard.hidden = false;
      if (f.type.startsWith('image/')) {
        thumbUrl = URL.createObjectURL(f);
        fileThumb.src = thumbUrl;
        fileThumb.alt = `Preview of ${f.name}`;
      } else {
        thumbUrl = null;
        fileThumb.removeAttribute('src');
        fileThumb.alt = 'No preview for this file type';
      }
      fileName.textContent = f.name;
      fileMeta.textContent = `${(f.size / 1024).toFixed(1)} KB · ${(f.name.split('.').pop() || '').toUpperCase()}${dimsText ? ` · ${dimsText}` : ''}`;
    }

    removeFile.addEventListener('click', () => {
      clearFile();
      resetResults();
      renderTrust();
      fileInput.focus();
    });

    function paintVerdict(pass, title, sub) {
      verdict.hidden = false;
      verdict.className = 'verdict ' + (pass ? 'pass' : 'fail');
      verdict.innerHTML = '';
      const t = document.createElement('p');
      t.className = 'v-title';
      t.textContent = title;
      const s = document.createElement('p');
      s.className = 'v-sub';
      s.textContent = sub;
      verdict.append(t, s);
    }

    function paintRows(rows) {
      ledger.hidden = false;
      resultsEmpty.hidden = true;
      ledgerBody.innerHTML = '';
      rows.forEach((r) => {
        const kind = r.pass == null ? 'info' : r.pass ? 'pass' : 'fail';
        const row = document.createElement('div');
        row.className = `report-row ${kind}`;
        const vals = document.createElement('div');
        vals.className = 'vals';
        const prop = document.createElement('span');
        prop.className = 'prop';
        prop.textContent = r.label.toUpperCase();
        const actual = document.createElement('div');
        actual.className = 'actual num';
        actual.textContent = r.actual;
        const req = document.createElement('div');
        req.className = 'req';
        req.textContent = r.expected;
        vals.append(prop, actual, req);
        const pill = document.createElement('span');
        pill.className = `pill ${kind}`;
        pill.textContent = kind === 'pass' ? '✓ PASS' : kind === 'fail' ? '✗ FAIL' : '• INFO';
        row.append(vals, pill);
        ledgerBody.appendChild(row);
      });
      updateMatchLine(rows);
    }

    async function handleFile() {
      const f = fileInput.files && fileInput.files[0];
      if (!f) return;
      if (!currentReq) {
        paintVerdict(false, '❌ Choose a form first', 'Pick your form in step 2, then upload again.');
        return;
      }
      currentFile = f;
      document.body.dataset.stage = 'file';
      delete document.body.dataset.result;
      updateProgress();
      if (fixedUrl) { URL.revokeObjectURL(fixedUrl); fixedUrl = null; }
      fixedBlob = null;
      downloadRow.hidden = true;
      beforeAfter.hidden = true;
      beforeImg.src = URL.createObjectURL(f);
      showFileCard(f);
      let props;
      try {
        props = await readFileProps(f);
      } catch (e) {
        paintVerdict(false, '❌ Could not read that file', `${e.message} Upload a JPG, JPEG or PNG image.`);
        return;
      }
      showFileCard(f, props.format === 'PDF' ? 'PDF document' : `${props.width} × ${props.height} px`);
      document.getElementById('bSize').textContent = `${props.sizeKB.toFixed(1)} KB`;
      document.getElementById('bDims').textContent = props.format === 'PDF' ? '—' : `${props.width} × ${props.height} px`;
      document.getElementById('bFormat').textContent = props.format;
      const rows = checkAgainstRequirement(props, currentReq);
      const fails = rows.filter((r) => r.pass === false);
      paintRows(rows);
      if (fails.length === 0) {
        paintVerdict(true, '✅ READY TO UPLOAD', `Your file meets the published requirements for ${currentReq.form_name}.`);
        document.body.dataset.result = 'pass';
        document.body.dataset.stage = 'result';
        fixBox.hidden = true;
      } else {
        paintVerdict(false, `⚠ ${fails.length} ISSUE${fails.length > 1 ? 'S' : ''} TO FIX`, 'Each failed row shows your file against the requirement.');
        document.body.dataset.result = 'fail';
        document.body.dataset.stage = 'result';
        const isPdf = f.type === 'application/pdf' || /pdf$/i.test(f.name);
        fixBox.hidden = false;
        fixBtn.disabled = isPdf;
        if (isPdf) {
          paintVerdict(false, `⚠ ${fails.length} ISSUE${fails.length > 1 ? 'S' : ''} TO FIX`, 'Automatic fix is not available for PDF files yet — convert to JPG first.');
        }
      }
      accuracyNote.textContent = `Meets the published requirements we verified as of ${currentReq.verified_date ?? 'an unverified date'}. The live portal is the final authority.`;
    }

    fileInput.addEventListener('change', handleFile);

    ['dragover', 'dragenter'].forEach((evt) => dropzone.addEventListener(evt, (e) => {
      if (fileInput.disabled) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      dropzone.classList.add('dz-active');
    }));
    dropzone.addEventListener('dragleave', () => dropzone.classList.remove('dz-active'));
    dropzone.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
      dropzone.classList.remove('dz-active');
      if (fileInput.disabled || !e.dataTransfer || !e.dataTransfer.files.length) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      fileInput.files = e.dataTransfer.files;
      handleFile();
    });

    fixBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      if (!currentFile || !currentReq) return;
      fixBtn.disabled = true;
      fixBtn.textContent = 'Fixing…';
      try {
        fixedBlob = await fixImage(currentFile, currentReq, (url) => { afterImg.src = url; });
        if (fixedUrl) URL.revokeObjectURL(fixedUrl);
        fixedUrl = URL.createObjectURL(fixedBlob);
        afterImg.src = fixedUrl;
        beforeAfter.hidden = false;
        const props = await readFileProps(new File([fixedBlob], 'fixed.jpg', { type: fixedBlob.type }));
        document.getElementById('aSize').textContent = `${(fixedBlob.size / 1024).toFixed(1)} KB`;
        document.getElementById('aDims').textContent = `${props.width} × ${props.height} px`;
        document.getElementById('aFormat').textContent = props.format;
        const rows = checkAgainstRequirement(props, currentReq);
        const fails = rows.filter((r) => r.pass === false);
        paintRows(rows);
        if (fails.length === 0) {
          paintVerdict(true, '✅ READY TO UPLOAD', `Fixed file is ${(fixedBlob.size / 1024).toFixed(1)} KB, corrected format and size.`);
          document.body.dataset.result = 'pass';
        } else {
          paintVerdict(false, `⚠ ${fails.length} ISSUE${fails.length > 1 ? 'S' : ''} REMAIN${fails.length > 1 ? '' : 'S'}`, 'The fixed file still differs on the rows marked FAIL — compare before and after below.');
          document.body.dataset.result = 'fail';
        }
        downloadRow.hidden = false;
        downloadBtn.disabled = false;
        downloadNote.textContent = '';
      } catch (e) {
        paintVerdict(false, '❌ Fix failed', `${e.message} Try a different file, or a smaller photo.`);
      } finally {
        fixBtn.disabled = false;
        fixBtn.textContent = 'Fix automatically';
      }
    });

    downloadBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!fixedBlob || !currentReq) return;
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = fixedUrl;
      a.download = `docheck-fixed-${currentReq.id}.jpg`;
      document.body.appendChild(a);
      a.click();
      a.remove();
      downloadNote.textContent = '✓ Download started — check your downloads folder.';
    });

    checkAnotherBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      clearFile();
      resetResults();
      renderTrust();
      updateProgress();
      fileInput.disabled = false;
      fileInput.focus();
    });
  </script>
</Base>
